{"title":"Chord","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>chord</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\">line segment</a> joining two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">points</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a989359a781a76d4c5b53cfaac7df1a5e010d89.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(100); pair O=origin,A=dir(135),B=dir(30); D(unitcircle); D(A--B); MP(&quot;O&quot;,D(O),S); MP(&quot;A&quot;,D(A),W); MP(&quot;B&quot;,D(B),E);[/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"155\" />\n</p><p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter\" title=\"Diameter\">diameter</a> of a circle is the longest chord of that circle. The diameter goes through the center of the circle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e236cfbd6b8f572926d159eeb35153c720466732.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]size(120); pair O=origin,A=dir(170),B=dir(-10); D(unitcircle); D(A--B); MP(&quot;O&quot;,D(O),N); MP(&quot;A&quot;,D(A),W); MP(&quot;B&quot;,D(B),E);[/asy]\" width=\"202\" height=\"162\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chord&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224339\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.010 seconds\nPr